```

The notes in the template:

```ts
// Result without the assertion: 1 passed
//
// Result with the assertion: 1 failed
//
// What changed between the two runs:
//   The website and the steps were the same, and the sign-in failed both
//   times. Only the second run checked the result, so only the second
//   run reported the failure.
```

**Why this problem matters.** An action such as `click` proves only that the step could be performed. It says nothing about whether the sign-in worked. Without an assertion, every test can pass while the website is broken.

